  },
  "question": {
    "text": "The diameter of the circle, whose Centre lies on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> in the first quadrant and which touches both the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Centre of circle lies on the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>Any point on the line can be assumed as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>So let Centre of circle is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Since both lines&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;touches the circle means distance from&nbsp;the Centre of circle to the line is equal to radius.</p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;is radius of circle.</p><p>For the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>For the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>&#945;</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>&#945;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Squaring both side</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>We know&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>&#945;</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Diameter<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}